### 3. Constructor Injection & DI Container

All dependencies are injected via constructor in [`FleetCoreEngine`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L440-L460):

```typescript
export interface FleetCoreDependencies {
  clock: IClock;
  random: IRandomGenerator;
  driverRepo: IDriverRepository;
  functionRepo: IFunctionCatalogRepository;
  hreRepo: IHreRestrictionRepository;
  telemetryProvider: ITraxxasTelemetryProvider;
  config: IFleetConfiguration;
}

export class FleetCoreEngine {
  private activeDriverId: string;

  constructor(private readonly deps: FleetCoreDependencies) {
    this.activeDriverId = deps.config.defaultDriverId;
  }

  // Public methods consume this.deps.clock, this.deps.driverRepo, this.deps.random, etc.
}
```

A DI container ([`FleetCoreContainer`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L650-L685)) and factory function `createFleetCore()` manage dependency resolution with production defaults ([`SystemClock`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L270-L278), [`DefaultRandomGenerator`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L280-L310), in-memory repositories). The default singleton instance `fleetCore` preserves the exact public API for [server.ts](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server.ts).

