### 1. Test Architecture & Environment Setup

The integration testing harness leverages the project’s native Node test stack ([`node:test`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/tests/api_integration.test.js), [`node:assert/strict`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/tests/api_integration.test.js), and native `fetch`):

- **Isolated Server Spawning**: [`createApiApp`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server.ts#L101-L154) exports the Express application factory decoupled from port listening and Vite dev middleware. An ephemeral HTTP server binds to dynamic port `0` (`127.0.0.1:0`), guaranteeing collision-free parallel or sequential runs.
- **Zero Shared Mutable State**: Each test context receives a fresh in-memory dependency injection container via [`createFleetCore()`](https://github.com/jeremiahjmorris1126-coder/TRUCKWITHEASE-1/blob/main/server/fleetCore.ts#L861-L872) with independent instances of `driverRepo`, `functionRepo`, `hreRepo`, and `telemetryProvider`. Test mutations never bleed across cases.
- **Traceability & Correlation**: All requests pass through correlation tracing (`x-correlation-id`), matching the TruckWithEase error-handling and telemetry taxonomy.

