### 2. Critical Endpoint Scenario Matrix

| Critical Endpoint | Happy Path Scenario | Validation Error Scenario | Auth / Permission Failure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`GET /api/health`** | Returns `200` with `UP`, `READY`, and active telecommunications gateway subsystem status. | N/A (no body payload required). | Whitelisted path; public telemetry probe without token requirement. |
| **`POST /api/auth/signup`** | Returns `201` with generated driver record, unit assignment, and safety rating. | Returns `400` with `E_DOMAIN_VALIDATION` if `fullName`, `cdlNumber`, or `fmcsaPin` is missing/malformed. | Rejects with `409` if CDL number is already registered across fleet. |
| **`POST /api/auth/signin`** | Returns `200` with authenticated driver session, CDL mask (`IL****20`), and active unit. | Returns `400` with `E_DOMAIN_VALIDATION` if neither CDL nor email is provided. | Returns `401` with `E_AUTH_PIN_MISMATCH` if 4-digit roadside PIN verification fails. |
| **`POST /api/drivers/select`** | Returns `200` confirming driver selection and synchronizing cab profile. | Returns `400` if `driverId` is empty or malformed UUID. | Returns `404` (`E_DOMAIN_NOT_FOUND`) when selecting a driver ID not in tenant roster. |
| **`POST /api/hre/route-audit`** | Returns `200` with clearance evaluation (e.g. Loop 820 safe for 14' 2" loads). | Returns `400` if vehicle height or corridor identifier is missing. | Returns `200` with `COLLISION RISK: CRITICAL` alert and bypass detour if bridge clearance buffer $\le 0$ inches. |
| **`GET /api/traxxas/telemetry`** | Returns `200` with 10Hz CAN-Bus vitals (engine RPM, oil pressure, kingpin angle). | N/A (query filter validation). | Returns `401` if Carrier API secret is required and missing. |
| **`POST /api/traxxas/ping`** | Returns `200` pong with CAN-Bus transponder status (`SYNCHRONIZED`). | Returns `400` on malformed ping payload. | Returns `401` when unauthorized tenant attempts transponder override. |
| **`POST /api/telecom/calls`** | Returns `201` voice call record, server ping acknowledgment, and toll rate ledger. | Returns `400` if recipient phone number is missing or not E.164 compliant. | Returns `401` without valid carrier token when secret enforcement is enabled. |
| **`POST /api/dispatch-messages`** | Returns `201` recording SMS directive and toll ledger debit (`$0.0079`/segment). | Returns `400` if `message` string is empty or exceeds character limits. | Returns `401` if unauthorized dispatch client posts to driver queue. |
| **`GET /api/telecom/summary`** | Returns `200` with carrier telecom balance, total calls, and toll ledger breakdown. | N/A (read-only audit). | Returns `401` if tenant token does not carry fleet accounting privileges. |
| **`Protected Carrier Routes`** *(e.g., Cloudflare export)* | Returns `200` when valid Bearer token matches `CARRIER_API_SECRET`. | Returns `400` on malformed header formatting. | Returns `401` (`Unauthorized`) when token is absent or invalid. |

